@bank all
// SW3 (2026-10-26, Pillar 5 Step 5, S5-3 words; spec section 10): M19 Power and relays (24v). The training is meeting
// train.m19.calder in the relay room (Deck 1, u); keys matched to B2's code (claude/p5s5-mech-a 3c38a65f, 2026-10-26):
// six relays R1-R6, a lamp that stutters; four battery cell pairs. Calder's tester line is her flag train.m19.tester; the
// crew's answers in the drill are content/banks/m19.lines. Said by nobody unless noted. No "!". Mails "Subject | body".

== works.mech.m19
- Power and relays
// the ask ({time}, {place} filled by the game)
== works.ask.m19
- Power and relays | Your first Senior training. The relay room, Deck 1. Bring your hands; I'll bring the relays. {time}, {place}.
== next.m19
- Power and relays comes next: the relay room on Deck 1, with the Chief.
== next.wait.m19
- Power and relays: meet the Chief in the relay room, Deck 1.
// the ring line on the arrow (B2's m19.ring), and the urgent notice at 10:30 (asks B2 for {name} and {time} too: the
// words check has no {ring})
== m19.ring
- Power and relays with {name}, {time}
== m19.notice
- Power and relays with {name} at {time}: {where}. Go at quarter to.

// the job cards on the board (B2's relayswap and battcell kinds)
== m19.card.relay
- Swap a failing relay: {place}
== m19.card.batt
- Check battery bank {n}
// the training's two looks (Calder's rack, 1-relay-1: you watch; {n} the stuttering relay's number)
== m19.train.open
- The rack hums. Six lamps. One stutters: R{n}. That's the one.
== m19.train.test
- Every lamp steady. Listen: it clicks over clean now.
// a relay rack: each lamp's word (in the list "R1 steady · R2 stutters ..."), the pick, a wrong pick, the test, done
== m19.relay.ok
- steady
== m19.relay.bad
- stutters
== m19.relay.pick
- Which relay's failing?
== m19.relay.wrong
- That one's steady. Watch the lamps again.
== m19.relay.test
- Every lamp steady.
== m19.relay.done
- Relay swapped. The rack's steady. The bridge won't flicker.
// a battery bank: four cell pairs ("Cells 1-2 green ..."), pick the low pair, swap the tired cell, check
== m19.batt.ok
- green
== m19.batt.low
- amber, sagging
== m19.batt.pick
- Which cells are low?
== m19.batt.wrong
- Those read fine. Look at the bars again.
== m19.batt.test
- All the bars green and level.
== m19.batt.done
- Bank {n}'s cells are level again.
// stage 2 (B2's turn 2, proposed): a conduit run with the conduit tester (6-conduit-1, -2)
== m19.conduit.title
- Conduit run · {machine}
== m19.conduit.test
- Test this length
== m19.conduit.good
- Clean all the way. Next length.
== m19.conduit.fault
- The tester drops here. The fault is in this length.
// the tester given (toast; only if M15 hasn't given it)
== m19.tester.give
- The Chief gave you a conduit tester. It's in your locker.
== m19.trained.stage2
- Power and relays: you can test conduit runs now.
== m19.trained.stage3
- Power and relays: the battery banks' balance is yours now.

// the drill (Wednesdays 15:00, once you're Senior): you run the Works part. The ring, the card, your calls
== drill.works.ptr
- Run the Works part of the drill
== drill.works.title
- The drill: Works
== drill.works.text
- You call Works' part. Three calls, in order. The crew answer on their devices.
== drill.works.call.1
- Works: all hands to your stations.
== drill.works.call.2
- Isolate the non-essential power. Report when done.
== drill.works.call.3
- Head count. Works, report in.
== drill.works.done
- Works reports all present and safe. Drill time: {time}.
== drill.works.order
- Not yet. Stations first, then power, then the count.
